IMPORT prelude

-- Coroners Act 1997 (ACT) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the prelude's date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library. The Act counts periods in days (ss 38, 55, 58A, 64, 68C, 90), months (ss 58A,
-- 76) and years (s 100).
--
-- READINGS (the Act does not say; the Legislation Act 2001, which governs the counting of time in ACT laws, is not
-- deposited and was not read): "n days after" a day is that day plus n; "n days before" a day is that day minus n; a
-- month or year after a day is the same day number that many months on, or the last day of the month where that month
-- is shorter (31 January plus 1 month is 28 or 29 February; 29 February plus 1 year is 28 February).
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Coroners Act 1997 (ACT)`

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`n` `days after` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`n` `days before` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` MINUS `n`)

GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `first` `is on or before` `second` IF DATE_SERIAL `first` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `second`

-- The number of days in month m of year y.
GIVEN `m` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day of month` `m` `y` MEANS
    IF `m` EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_DAY (DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (`m` PLUS 1) `y`) MINUS 1))

-- "n months after" a day (n a whole number, 0 or more).
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`n` `months after` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY `the day number` `the new month` `the new year`
    WHERE
        `months from January` MEANS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS `n`
        `the new month` MEANS (`months from January` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `the new year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS ((`months from January` MINUS (`months from January` MODULO 12)) DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the day number` MEANS
            IF DATE_DAY `the day` AT MOST `the last day of month` `the new month` `the new year`
            THEN DATE_DAY `the day`
            ELSE `the last day of month` `the new month` `the new year`

-- "n years after" a day.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`n` `years after` `the day` MEANS (`n` TIMES 12) `months after` `the day`
